<statement>
<p>
	This function controls the overall flow of one full game and returns the final state of this game.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>state</pf> (1 x 1) number — struct object representing an initialized state.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>state</pf> (1 x 1) number — struct object containing the final state.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>The tasks of this function are as follows:</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell>
			<p>
				<ul>
					<li>Loop as long as the game is not over.</li>
					<li>Wait for the player to click on a space.</li>
					<li>Determine if the click was a left or right click.</li>
					<li>If the click was "valid" (via a helper function).</li>
					<li>Process the left or right-click (via helper functions).</li>
					<li>Check for a game over state (via a helper function).</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Follow the template provided in class.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
